e92408a4 (2449 1792769587055 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f313p4") (src . "context: a text file's library and imports are read from its header, no-library definitions are scoped by file, ambiguity is folded, and the caller may name what the edit will use\n\nA Scheme file stored in text mode had no library: the splitter's cuts fall\ninside the one library form, so every piece was `in-library none`, every\ndefinition reached every user through def-for's no-library clause, and a\ncontext answer for a code block was dozens of `(ambiguous)` candidates for\none-letter names before anything else. Now:\n\n- (theourgia reader), a new library below store and name-use: a small bounded\n  reader for the header prefix and for complete forms (limits on bytes, depth\n  and form count, numbers kept opaque), and the one spelling of a library\n  name proper.\n- A text-mode file's library and imports are read from its header through\n  the file holder (the srcs of its code children in document order, up to\n  65536 bytes); `in-library`, `imports`, `file-imports` and the scope-name\n  rules read that name; the definitions index is built through it. A header\n  the reader refuses, or a first piece that is not UTF-8, is no header, and\n  nothing on that path raises (the catch-all guard around the header read is\n  gone).\n- `holder`, a stored fact: a code block and its file holder; def-for's\n  no-library clause requires the same holder, so a script's own top-level\n  definitions are in scope for its own pieces and for nothing else.\n- uses-name for a text-mode block of a language with a reader binds what its\n  complete forms bind, with the contract `(syntactic (reading forms))` and\n  a reason when the text does not read; the quasiquote walk is iterative over\n  the list spine.\n- context folds a name's definitions past the first two into a `folded`\n  clause; `--names <n>` (repeatable) enters a name's definitions in the\n  target's scope ahead of the preferred steps, reported in `asked`; a holder\n  or any non-code target scopes to the code blocks under it; `--budget\n  min+<t>` resolves to the minimum plus room and the answer shows the number.\n- The session trace carries, per call, defs-index builds, fact builds by\n  relation, preferred candidates by step, and whether the session was reused\n  or why it was dropped (state moved, external stratum, catalogue generation).\n- Rows in test/context-targeting.sc (56); seven existing fixtures follow the\n  scope change; platform-rows and daemon-link-gate counts and commit-premises'\n  with-store-write file list move for the new file and the new row; README\n  sections for context, the relation tables, name-use's contract and the\n  trace.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 458))))
